// Brokkr-managed — installed by scripts/setup-host-patching.sh only onto the Debian /
// Raspberry Pi OS hosts the owner approved in BROKKR_REGULAR_UPDATE_HOSTS (Grimnir
// ADR-009: regular OS updates, guarded reboots). Any other host gets the security
// baseline only, and the script removes this file from it.
//
// apt merges list-valued options across apt.conf.d files, so these patterns are
// appended to the security-only baseline in 50unattended-upgrades. Origins:
//   * Debian stable          - point releases (bug fixes the security archive lacks).
//   * Debian stable-updates  - the "-updates" archive (tzdata, clamav, other fixes).
//   * Raspberry Pi archive   - carries the Pi kernel, firmware and rpi-eeprom; it is
//                              not part of the Debian-Security origin.
//   * gh                     - the GitHub CLI repository (stable channel).
// Every repository is matched by exact origin, label and codename / channel; a
// channel that is not listed here is never admitted. Debian-family hosts have no
// Tailscale apt repository, so none is listed. A pattern that matches no
// configured repository is a no-op, so one file serves every approved Debian-family
// host whatever subset of these repositories it has.
// Reboots are never done here; see the guarded-reboot job and 50unattended-upgrades.
Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern {
        "origin=Debian,codename=${distro_codename},label=Debian";
        "origin=Debian,codename=${distro_codename}-updates,label=Debian";
        "origin=Raspberry Pi Foundation,codename=${distro_codename},label=Raspberry Pi Foundation";
        "origin=gh,label=gh,codename=stable";
};
